env/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.nfs*
sativa_epang/raxml/raxmlHPC8-*
config.local.sh

# Derived from results/runs, regenerated in seconds by the scripts, so kept out of git:
results/report.html
results/concordance_details.tsv
results/concordance_vs_gamma_details.tsv
results/**/stdout.log
# score.json is score_injection.py's per-cell output, written back into the run directory. Derived
# from the .mis and the cell's truth.json, which are both committed, and rebuilt for all 854 cells
# in seconds by bin/analyses.sh. Spot-checked byte-identical against the cluster's copies.
results/**/score.json

# The per-cell datasets, rebuilt from their seeds by slurm/make_grid.sh and slurm/make_foreign.sh with
# no cluster and no container. 92 MB on disk: 62 MB under data/injected, almost all of it .tax, and
# 30 MB for the nine foreign cells, whose .fasta carry appended donors and are real files.
#
# An injected cell's .fasta is a symlink to data/gtdb/gtdb_arc2k.fasta, because injection rewrites a
# taxonomy and never an alignment, so there is one alignment on disk and not 180. This comment once
# said 86 MB, which was right -- it measured the disk. A review then "corrected" it to 642 MB by
# summing os.path.getsize over the symlinks, which counts one 3 MB file 180 times, and accused the
# original of being wrong by a factor of seven while being wrong by that factor itself. What is
# committed is the truth.json each cell is scored against, and data/README.md records the check that
# all 378 regenerate byte-identically.
data/injected/*/*.tax
data/injected/*/*.fasta
data/foreign/*/*.tax
data/foreign/*/*.fasta
work/
.nextflow/
.nextflow.log*
results/nf/

# The generators redirect their stderr per cell into warn.txt. 225 of them were committed, all
# empty, while a full regeneration writes a real note into 90 -- a committed record asserting that no
# cell warned when half of them do. The note is a transcript; the record is truth.json, which carries
# n_requested, n_injected and rate_effective for every cell.
warn.txt
